    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f3d56a5f-d951-5759-bedd-eb722dd00798" activityNameId="31e0bc9b-9caf-5e79-a0b3-c8315bc6eb23" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Keyboard, wireless version, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Keyboard, wireless version, at plant
The dataset is made from the existing average keyboards; UUID: 5382c34f-c048-39e3-9ded-28d4006322be
The wireless keyboard is modeled using the existing wired keyboard dataset. The modifications to the existing keyboards include the addition of a pair NiMh batteries (50 grams), the removal of wired cable, and lastly the increased mass of PCB components (Babbitt et al., 2020). The rest of other inventory flows are assumed to be the same as optimized wired keyboards - see the mentioned dataset.
Location: Data for global average wireless keyboards
Technology: The production of a computer keyboard includes the electroplating process of the steel base sheet with zinc plus the injection moulding of the ABS-plastic parts (upper and lower shell; wheel).
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Literature data and own assumptions for processing calculations.
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: see Geography and Technology
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5382c34f-c048-39e3-9ded-28d4006322be.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
